  "title": "08 · 理论脉络与综合认识",
  "scope": "Reorganizes existing results into a review of their theoretical roles and conditional connections. Replaces the earlier evidence-hierarchy, independent-measurement and intervention-focused main structure.",
  "structure": [
    "1. Introduction: resource axes and distinct explanatory tasks",
    "2. Static origins: Bahri, geometry/spectra, Bordelon/Canatar, Maloney and Michaud",
    "3. Fixed representation to feature learning",
    "4. Controlled graph tests and compute scaling as consequences of risk relations",
    "5. Shared understanding, model scope and state of the theory",
    "6. References"
  ],
  "connections": {
    "variance_resolution": "Fixed-complexity statistical correction versus an optimized complexity envelope within a stated two-term proxy; not claimed as the exact formula for every Bahri regime.",
    "geometry_spectrum": "Explicit uniform-torus Sobolev projection upper bound and conditional radial Fourier-kernel eigenvalue ordering; target regularity and kernel smoothness remain distinct. Bounds are not promoted to exact universal exponents.",
    "random_features": "Joint latent Gaussian/random-feature structure; teacher averaging, N,D below latent rank, noiseless/unregularized exchange symmetry and its noise limitation. Gram spectra alone are not used to prove arbitrary risk duality.",
    "skills_spectrum": "Shared positive Laplace representation under stated assumptions, with optimization rate/target energy distinguished from appearance frequency/test usage. Capacity and sample mappings differ.",
    "feature_learning": "Uses the same initial source-condition notation as the kernel model; rich hard-task time exponent is model-specific, while the fixed projection retains the capacity bottleneck and finite-data limits.",
    "computation": "Optimizing a supplied risk surface under a supplied cost is a consequence/application layer, not another microscopic origin theory."
  },
